<aura:documentation>
    <aura:description>
        <h1>Documentation for Siloed Info Related Record Display</h1>
        <p>This component will allow administrators to drop it in place on a lightning app page and select a field set that will be displayed to the user from a related object. For example on the account this component can display specific information from the parent account. Administrators can configure:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><em>Title</em>: The title of the component on the page</li>
            <li><em>Number Of Columns</em>: The number of columns that are displayed</li>
            <li><em>Record Mode</em>: The record mode includes three options for the user to interact with the fields
                <ol>
                    <li>View: The component loads in a view state and allows for inline editing</li>
                    <li>Edit: The component loads in an edit state</li>
                    <li>Read Only: The component loads in a read only state and cannot be edited by the user</li>
                </ol>
            </li>
            <li><em>Logo</em>: Allows the user to select a logo that is displayed for that component from the standard Salesforce logos</li>
            <li><em>Field to Lookup Against</em>: The API Name of the lookup field and fieldset API name for its object with a : as the dilimeter, e.g. on the Account object ParentId:Test_FS</li>
        </ul>
    </aura:description>
</aura:documentation>